-- [[ LOCAL SCRIPT: Inventory UI (Optimized v5 - Production) ]]
--      - UI pooling (no destroy/recreate spam)
--      - Event-driven inventory tracking (fast updates)
--      - No per-item Heartbeat loops (Tweens instead)
--      - FIXED: Backpack/Character respawn logic (Critical)
--      - Keeps: dynamic FOV, xCount, mobile friendly, universal glow
--
-- ============================================================
-- FIX LOG (v4)
-- FIX #1–#18: see previous version notes
-- ============================================================
-- FIX LOG (v5 — Production Hardening)
-- FIX #19 Inventory item drag initiation now checks `isOpen` before
--         starting a drag. Prevents ghost drags when the inventory
--         GUI is closed but buttons are still technically alive.
-- FIX #20 performClose() cancels any in-flight drag via endDrag(false)
--         so closing the inventory never leaves a dangling drag icon.
-- FIX #21 Hotbar car-name labels now display the fantasy car name
--         (the CarStats key, e.g. "Centurion") with a rarity-coloured
--         gradient. getDisplayName() centralises the lookup.
-- FIX #22 updateHotbarUI sanitization is also triggered immediately
--         inside ChildRemoved with a direct visual sweep, ensuring
--         icons for lost cars vanish in the same frame.
-- FIX #23 getDisplayName() centralises the key→display-name lookup
--         so every label site is consistent.
-- FIX #24 Drag threshold increased to 12px and touch hold delay to
--         0.65s for better cross-device feel.
-- FIX #25 ENTIRE ChildRemoved hotbar logic is now DEFERRED by one
--         frame. When a tool moves between Backpack↔Character
--         (equip/unequip), ChildRemoved fires first (count→0), then
--         ChildAdded fires (count→1). Both the direct sweep AND the
--         updateHotbarUI sanitization would see count=0 and
--         incorrectly clear hotbar slots. Deferring lets the companion
--         ChildAdded restore the count first. If count is still 0
--         after the defer, the car is truly gone and slots are cleared.
-- FIX #26 Drop handler's post-drop render is now DEFERRED by one frame
--         and sets refreshQueued=true to block stale pending renders.
--         This ensures FIX #25's deferred ChildRemoved sweep and any
--         ChildAdded scheduleRender settle before the final authoritative
--         render paints the definitive post-drop UI state.
-- FIX #27 Hotbar name labels now use an animated gradient system that
--         matches the inventory's setGlow — same rarity color sequences,
--         tilted gradient, black stroke, and looping shimmer tween.
-- FIX #28 CarInfoLabel inside each hotbar slot now displays the car's
--         base CPS from CarStats. Formatted as +5M$/s, +833.7K$/s, etc.
-- ============================================================
-- FIX LOG (v6 — Mobile-Safe Inventory)
-- FIX #29 Removed destructive mobile long-press clear on hotbar slots.
--         Touch hold no longer removes cars. Use right-click/gamepad/drag
--         to inventory for intentional clearing.
-- FIX #30 Inventory item source buttons are never hidden at drag start.
--         This prevents mobile long-press/touch-cancel from making an item
--         look like it disappeared from the inventory.
-- FIX #31 Inventory renders no longer skip the currently dragged car.
--         Display count remains authoritative and visible unless a drop
--         actually succeeds.
-- FIX #32 Hotbar drags no longer clear hotbarData before the drop is
--         confirmed. Failed/cancelled mobile drags cannot lose slot data.
-- FIX #33 endDrag() performs a final safe visual refresh so cancelled
--         drags recover immediately.
-- ============================================================

